---
# infra-copilot:customization start
backend: object-storage        # required: hcp | object-storage; confirm the choice during setup
leaf_backends: {}               # declared leaf overrides; e.g. {github: object-storage} with default hcp
github_org: your-org
apex_domain: example.dev
cloudflare_account_id: 0000000000000000000000000000000
cloudflare_zone_id: 0000000000000000000000000000000
managed_repos:
  - your-org/infra
# ── HCP fields (when any effective leaf is hcp, including overrides) ─────────
# hcp_org: your-org
# hcp_status_check_id: ""

# ── Object-storage fields (when any effective leaf is object-storage) ────────
state_backend: gcs             # gcs | s3 | azurerm; choose your storage provider
state_bucket: your-org-tf-state
state_prefix: terraform/state
# state_lock_table: ""         # DynamoDB table for S3; GCS/azurerm have native locking
# state_region: ""             # for S3 backend and Azure resource group creation; GCS uses bucket location
# azure_storage_account: ""    # storage account name for azurerm backend
# azure_resource_group: ""     # resource group for azurerm backend

additional_providers: []
# Replace [] when adopting a provider.
#
# HCP mode example:
# additional_providers:
#   - name: gcp
#     workspace: gcp
#     mise_tools:
#       - gcloud
#     mise_config_blob: ""
#     mise_lock_blob: ""
#     fork_speculative_plans_disabled: false
#     fork_speculative_plans_workspace_id: ""
#     credentials_verified_at: ""
#     credentials_backend: ""
#     credential_variables:
#       - key: TFC_GCP_PROVIDER_AUTH
#         category: env
#         sensitive: false
#       - key: TFC_GCP_PRINCIPAL_TYPE
#         category: env
#         sensitive: false
#       - key: TFC_GCP_RUN_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL
#         category: env
#         sensitive: false
#       - key: TFC_GCP_WORKLOAD_PROVIDER_NAME
#         category: env
#         sensitive: false
#
# Object-storage mode example:
# additional_providers:
#   - name: gcp
#     mise_tools:
#       - gcloud
#     mise_config_blob: ""
#     mise_lock_blob: ""
#     credentials_verified_at: ""
#     credentials_backend: ""
#     credential_secrets: []  # WIF identifiers are public; configure them in the workflow
# infra-copilot:customization end
---

# infra-copilot config

Public identifiers for this repo. Copy to `.infra-copilot/config.md`, fill in
your org's values, and commit.

Object-storage is the recommended starting choice. Confirm it during setup, or set
`backend: hcp` and fill in the HCP fields instead. Always record the choice explicitly;
omitting `backend` stops every action skill before checks run. For an existing HCP repo,
add `backend: hcp` to preserve its current workflow.
HCP mode requires a paid tier with team management for the mandatory plan-only team
token, even below the free tier's 500-resource limit; see the backend comparison in
[`config.md`](config.md#backend-modes).

- **HCP mode**: Secrets live in HCP workspace variables.
- **Object-storage mode**: Secrets live in GitHub Actions secrets.

Keep the two `infra-copilot:customization` comments. Everything between them is
yours; a re-scaffold preserves it verbatim and rewrites only the rest. Delete or
unbalance them and a re-scaffold has no way to tell your values from the
template, so it stops and hands off instead of guessing.

## Staged backend migration

`backend` is the explicit default. Override only the migrating declared leaf in
`leaf_backends`, for example `github: object-storage` while `backend: hcp` remains.
Synchronize `GITHUB_BACKEND` in both plan and apply workflows in that leaf's cutover PR;
keep the other leaves' routes, workspace connections, credentials and protection intact.
Setup/status select the effective routes, including both services in mixed mode.
Their checks verify routing and execution evidence, not the human state-transfer gates.
Follow the hub skill's packaged `references/docs/object-storage-state.md`
("Migrating from HCP") for each leaf's cutover. Neither skipped checks nor a green
mixed-backend scan replaces verified state transfer, retired HCP writers and an approved
destination apply. Review all inherited routes before changing the repository default.
